WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.895
Your team presents the same onboarding deck to every new starter.

2
00:00:04.945 --> 00:00:10.225
What if they could watch it on day one, at their own pace, with the same message every time?

3
00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:13.965
Start by sorting your decks into three groups.

4
00:00:14.015 --> 00:00:22.141
Stable policies and company history suit video, things that change often stay out, and welcomes and Q&A stay live.

5
00:00:22.641 --> 00:00:28.233
A new hire is more likely to finish five six-minute videos than one thirty-minute video.

6
00:00:28.283 --> 00:00:31.451
So split your content into short, focused topics.

7
00:00:32.041 --> 00:00:33.825
Tidy each deck first.

8
00:00:33.875 --> 00:00:40.294
Give every slide one idea and a headline that makes a point, and swap stale names for roles like your manager.

9
00:00:41.441 --> 00:00:46.802
Your speaker notes become the voiceover, so write them like you're explaining things to a new colleague.

10
00:00:46.852 --> 00:00:49.764
Keep sentences short and spell out acronyms.

11
00:00:50.841 --> 00:00:54.739
When a policy changes, just edit the slide and convert again.

12
00:00:54.789 --> 00:00:59.603
On Pro, a.i. directs each video so it lands like a produced welcome.

13
00:00:59.653 --> 00:01:02.972
Try Basic first at powerpoint2vid.com.

